{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals","id":1554906,"title":"3e Sidereals: Better infernalists than Infernals?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-31T18:40:27-07:00","id":1554906,"title":"3e Sidereals: Better infernalists than Infernals?","content":"A discussion on another forum suddenly made me dwell on a point that really sums up my major concern with 3e Infernal Charm design. 3e Sidereals includes a Charm called Chains of Adorjan in which a Sidereal can command <b>an actual manifestation of Adorjan </b>in battle, in the form of a deadly vortex. This is far and away the most direct form of Yozi intervention in Creation portrayed in the setting so far. The Charm even specifies she can see through it and fall in love (a bad thing, of course!) just to make clear this is a portion of the actual entity.<br /> <br /> It also opens the distressing precedent in terms of Charm design that there could be other Sidereal Charms directly invoking the power of the Yozis. Somewhere in Yu-Shan there might be a Sidereal who calls on the ever-reliable advice of his friend the Ebon Dragon to look for tax loopholes, or a Chosen of Serenity who manifests Malfeas as a ballroom to perfect dance beyond mortal limit<br /> <br /> This is concerning to me because the most consistent thing I've heard about 3e Infernals is that the Yozis are supposed to be de-emphasised in their Charm design. That they are not using Yozi Charms, that they are lesser in terms of communion with their fallen titan sponsors. And I've always questioned what that actually contributes to the <i>fun </i>of playing Infernals. Now I question what the point even was when Sidereals can literally tag team a Yozi to come attack an Infernal-which on it's own, is fine, Adorjan is not known for mercy towards her allies. It's just shocking to me this is a <b>Sidereal Charm </b>while Infernals aren't even allowed to touch<b> real </b>Yozi power. I truly hope I'm missing something here as the kickstarter looms nearer, because on the face of things while it IS an intensely cool Charm, it is just baffling to me that Sidereals are allowed to use a Charm that is literally a more direct conduit to Yozi power than every non-RotS published 2e Infernal Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T01:59:29-07:00","id":1554911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Organ Boy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals#post1554906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A discussion on another forum suddenly made me dwell on a point that really sums up my major concern with 3e Infernal Charm design. 3e Sidereals includes a Charm called Chains of Adorjan in which a Sidereal can command <b>an actual manifestation of Adorjan </b>in battle, in the form of a deadly vortex. This is far and away the most direct form of Yozi intervention in Creation portrayed in the setting so far. The Charm even specifies she can see through it and fall in love (a bad thing, of course!) just to make clear this is a portion of the actual entity.<br /> <br /> It also opens the distressing precedent in terms of Charm design that there could be other Sidereal Charms directly invoking the power of the Yozis. Somewhere in Yu-Shan there might be a Sidereal who calls on the ever-reliable advice of his friend the Ebon Dragon to look for tax loopholes, or a Chosen of Serenity who manifests Malfeas as a ballroom to perfect dance beyond mortal limit<br /> <br /> This is concerning to me because the most consistent thing I've heard about 3e Infernals is that the Yozis are supposed to be de-emphasised in their Charm design. That they are not using Yozi Charms, that they are lesser in terms of communion with their fallen titan sponsors. And I've always questioned what that actually contributes to the <i>fun </i>of playing Infernals. Now I question what the point even was when Sidereals can literally tag team a Yozi to come attack an Infernal-which on it's own, is fine, Adorjan is not known for mercy towards her allies. It's just shocking to me this is a <b>Sidereal Charm </b>while Infernals aren't even allowed to touch<b> real </b>Yozi power. I truly hope I'm missing something here as the kickstarter looms nearer, because on the face of things while it IS an intensely cool Charm, it is just baffling to me that Sidereals are allowed to use a Charm that is literally a more direct conduit to Yozi power than every non-RotS published 2e Infernal Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>For one thing, Chains of Adorjan isn't a 3e original. 1e and 2e had it as a resplendent effect, long before the Infernals were a twinkle in anyone's eye. Now that it's a Sid Charm, there's one important thing to keep in mind: the Maidens sign off on Sid Charms. If they don't want their Chosen summoning any other Yozis, then they're not going to be able to summon any other Yozis.<br /> <br /> 3e Infernals are more distanced from their Yozi sponsors... but only to the extent that they can't use their Charms. They <i>are</i> still damn well capable of drawing on the Yozis' power, being able to start creating soul pantheons and inner worlds from the get-go. That's not coming from the Solar Exaltation, that's coming from the Essence of Hell that suffuses it. Not to mention 2e Infernals had to wait until Essence 6 to do that.<br /> <br /> Sidereals <i>don't get anything like that</i>. Summoning Adorjan is <u>all</u> they get, and all they <u>can</u> get. 3e Infernals get to emulate the Yozis' nature right from the start.<br /> <br /> If your Infernal power fantasy was being able to use the Yozis' Charms, then yes, you're going to be disappointed by 3e Infernals. Nevertheless, it's still going to be clear they're mainlining the Yozis' power, partaking of their nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T20:09:38-07:00","id":1554933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1554911#post1554911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For one thing, Chains of Adorjan isn't a 3e original. 1e and 2e had it as a resplendent effect, long before the Infernals were a twinkle in anyone's eye. Now that it's a Sid Charm, there's one important thing to keep in mind: the Maidens sign off on Sid Charms. If they don't want their Chosen summoning any other Yozis, then they're not going to be able to summon any other Yozis.<br /> <br /> 3e Infernals are more distanced from their Yozi sponsors... but only to the extent that they can't use their Charms. They <i>are</i> still damn well capable of drawing on the Yozis' power, being able to start creating soul pantheons and inner worlds from the get-go. That's not coming from the Solar Exaltation, that's coming from the Essence of Hell that suffuses it. Not to mention 2e Infernals had to wait until Essence 6 to do that.<br /> <br /> Sidereals <i>don't get anything like that</i>. Summoning Adorjan is <u>all</u> they get, and all they <u>can</u> get. 3e Infernals get to emulate the Yozis' nature right from the start.<br /> <br /> If your Infernal power fantasy was being able to use the Yozis' Charms, then yes, you're going to be disappointed by 3e Infernals. Nevertheless, it's still going to be clear they're mainlining the Yozis' power, partaking of their nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is rather cold comfort to me when I'm deeply perplexed by how &quot;can't use their Charms&quot; isn't, by definition, objectively more distanced. It is extremely frustrating to me that the emulation of Yozi nature is somehow being depicted as in any way, shape or form an upgrade <b>narratively </b>over the idea of actually channeling the powers that created the setting and conquered the Wyld. Yes, mechanically speaking the idea of being able to do soul pantheons and inner worlds from the get-go is absolutely welcome, but it all rings a bit hollow when there's no substance, no jump-off point, no narrative continuation to it. You might as well be told your compensation to no longer using actual Yozi Charms is getting to become a Yozi-themed Unshaped. <br /> <br /> It's a frustrating thought exercise because so much of Infernal design has been opaque and seemingly changed over time so it's difficult to say anything definitive, but when the consistent emphasis I've heard is a move away from transhumanism it's difficult not to be pessimistic when Alchemicals certainly get something to look forward to over the millennia in terms of leaving behind their humanity. Summoning Adorjan is something I would've imagine would be a &quot;conventional Elder Essence Infernal Charm in 2e, so it's very disheartening to see that alongside the repeated emphasis that Infernals are moving away from everything that made playing one engaging and replaced by, frankly, a Green Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T23:51:31-07:00","id":1554943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1554911#post1554911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For one thing, Chains of Adorjan isn't a 3e original. 1e and 2e had it as a resplendent effect, long before the Infernals were a twinkle in anyone's eye. Now that it's a Sid Charm, there's one important thing to keep in mind: the Maidens sign off on Sid Charms. If they don't want their Chosen summoning any other Yozis, then they're not going to be able to summon any other Yozis.<br /> <br /> 3e Infernals are more distanced from their Yozi sponsors... but only to the extent that they can't use their Charms. They <i>are</i> still damn well capable of drawing on the Yozis' power, being able to start creating soul pantheons and inner worlds from the get-go. That's not coming from the Solar Exaltation, that's coming from the Essence of Hell that suffuses it. Not to mention 2e Infernals had to wait until Essence 6 to do that.<br /> <br /> Sidereals <i>don't get anything like that</i>. Summoning Adorjan is <u>all</u> they get, and all they <u>can</u> get. 3e Infernals get to emulate the Yozis' nature right from the start.<br /> <br /> If your Infernal power fantasy was being able to use the Yozis' Charms, then yes, you're going to be disappointed by 3e Infernals. Nevertheless, it's still going to be clear they're mainlining the Yozis' power, partaking of their nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also having had time to look up the Charm in both editions, it just makes me all the more baffled why they thought Infernals had to stop using Yozi Charms in the first place when apparently this was considered A-OK for Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T11:00:35-08:00","id":1554977,"title":"","content":"Because those two things are worlds apart?<br /> <br /> &quot;Summon a fragment of Adorjan to do stuff on the battlefield&quot; is the same as walking into Cecelyne and scooping a bucket of her sand up to do ritual stuff with. It's not communing with her or even, really, *commanding* her to do anything. The only thing it represents is Heaven's very small authority over the prison of Malfeas.<br /> <br /> Channeling the Yozi's Charms was changed for several reasons.<br /> 1) It meant you couldn't design Charms that fit your Infernal. Even if they could do so accidentally, the actual design constraint is whether they fit the Yozi. (I know people largely ignored this to create Charms Of Therapy for the Yozi, but the text's intent is pretty strong.)<br /> 2) It meant every Charm had to be evaluated for what it &quot;said about the Yozi&quot; on some grander setting level, and that's just not a useful thing to saddle Charms with as a design restriction.<br /> 3) It limited what you could pull from. Malfeas had to build an entire sub-tree just to start *gesturing* to Ligier-themed Charms, rather than just... being able to plonk some Ligier Charms down directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but it all rings a bit hollow when there's no substance, no jump-off point, no narrative continuation to it. </div> </div> </div>This is a really extreme thing to leap to from a frankly not-that-significant slight metaphysical twibble to the Charmset.<br /> <br /> If &quot;using the Yozi's actual Charms&quot; was really this load-bearing of a pillar for you then, as mentioned, yes, 3e will not satisfy you, but I think you're ascribing a lot more value to that concept than was ever really there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/396-mr-rage","name":"Mr Rage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T06:54:41-08:00","id":1555022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Rage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1554977#post1554977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because those two things are worlds apart?<br /> <br /> &quot;Summon a fragment of Adorjan to do stuff on the battlefield&quot; is the same as walking into Cecelyne and scooping a bucket of her sand up to do ritual stuff with. It's not communing with her or even, really, *commanding* her to do anything. The only thing it represents is Heaven's very small authority over the prison of Malfeas.<br /> <br /> Channeling the Yozi's Charms was changed for several reasons.<br /> 1) It meant you couldn't design Charms that fit your Infernal. Even if they could do so accidentally, the actual design constraint is whether they fit the Yozi. (I know people largely ignored this to create Charms Of Therapy for the Yozi, but the text's intent is pretty strong.)<br /> 2) It meant every Charm had to be evaluated for what it &quot;said about the Yozi&quot; on some grander setting level, and that's just not a useful thing to saddle Charms with as a design restriction.<br /> 3) It limited what you could pull from. Malfeas had to build an entire sub-tree just to start *gesturing* to Ligier-themed Charms, rather than just... being able to plonk some Ligier Charms down directly.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a really extreme thing to leap to from a frankly not-that-significant slight metaphysical twibble to the Charmset.<br /> <br /> If &quot;using the Yozi's actual Charms&quot; was really this load-bearing of a pillar for you then, as mentioned, yes, 3e will not satisfy you, but I think you're ascribing a lot more value to that concept than was ever really there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really say any of these were really meaningful hurdles to me, in practice. Also the point I'm making is that small authority to command that facet of Adorjan <i>is more ability to express her nature than 3e Infernals will ever have, simply because Adorjan is by definition using Adorjan Charms.</i><br /> <br /> 1) In many ways, I enjoyed the unique relationship between Yozi Charms and Infernals because Infernals worked around their Charms instead of the other way around. It really sold the &quot;damnation and hellfire&quot; experience. Even within that purview, it was mentioned in Charms such as Scouring Banishment Technique that were facets of even existing Charms awaiting invention. Even if you don't want to go full Devil-Tiger, I felt that alone was an interesting avenue for Charm innovation: To take the themes of the Yozis, and reinvent them in response to your own needs or insights instead of theirs.<br /> 2) I don't feel that saddled the design of Charms at all. Malfeas is a complex fella. A grand craftsman, dancer and even statesmen. The themes of the Yozis are broad enough I always got the takeaway there was more to them than the most obvious, rage and torment-expressing facets to explore.<br /> 3) I don't see how that limits Charm design anymore than Solar Melee limits you to, well, swinging a sword around. I mean look at Essence, many of the same Charms are still being used to do basic concepts like &quot;set your weapon on hellfire&quot;, and yes I'm aware Essence is supposedly not representative of Infernals in their endstate. But it is if nothing else an illustration of how I'm unsure how the themes of the Yozis are a limit on Charm innovation at all.<br /> <br /> And yes, I'm ascribing a lot of value to the concept so innovative I still own pages and pages of homebrew dedicated to fleshing it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T08:54:51-08:00","id":1555027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Organ Boy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1554933#post1554933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is extremely frustrating to me that the emulation of Yozi nature is somehow being depicted as in any way, shape or form an upgrade <b>narratively </b>over the idea of actually channeling the powers that created the setting and conquered the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your attachment to this thing is based on the perception of it having this kind of prestige, then it's not really great for emphasizing the Exalted characters.<br /> <br /> And just a general issue of serial escalation. Like, you're getting wildly out of proportion when it's reached the point of &quot;anything less than being actual God isn't worth it&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Infernal Exalted deserve to be impressive in their own right.<br /> <br /> As for the thread title question, no, a single example of Sidereal esoteric weirdness in the form of invoking Adorjan as a death effect does not make the Sidereal Exalted more evocative of this setting's Hell than the characters who are going to express demonic and Yozi qualities across the entire range of their powers. That would be like looking at the one Solar Charm to let them turn into a shadow and saying they're better at darkness than Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T06:44:55-08:00","id":1555056,"title":"","content":"I think I can see the issue that the OP sees, albeit I don't necessarily agree. I have a problem of extremes here:<br /> <br /> 2e Infernals were practically extensions of the Yozi that had to paint their individuality with the colours they were given (so to speak). That <i>does </i>give an &quot;infernal&quot; feel in that you're an extensions of the &quot;gods of hell&quot; (so to speak), but Infernals were supposed to have free will - you had the Akuma for being an extension of Yozi will. I can see how one would want Infernals to be &quot;impressive on their own right&quot;.<br /> <br /> But if the proposed solution it's doing a 180\u00b0, and trying to be as sepparate from the Yozi as possible, &quot;Yozi like but having <i>as little </i>to do with the actual Yozi as possible&quot;, then I would agree with the OP: That doesn't feel very &quot;infernal&quot; to me. I wouldn't like if Yozi get ignored, after all, they are the demon-gods. They're Hell itself. Every demon has something to do with them. They're important to the Lore in ways the average demon isn't (that they were the original creators of the world that want to come back it's <i>interesting</i>), being a disconnected &quot;Yozi-like creature&quot; is hardly going to fell as badass to me.<br /> <br /> That being said, I do think it's possible to get that &quot;prestigious infernal feel&quot; w/o needing to go back to 2ed where you were defined by your chosen Yozi patrons.<br /> <br /> Heck, the very OP proves it: Does summoning a manifestation of a Yozi suffices to make Siderals feel like &quot;good Infernalists&quot;? ... well, why shouldn't Infernals be able to do things like that? (<i>not the</i> <i>same thing</i>, mind you, but akin to it - ways to &quot;manifest/take power from Hell itself&quot;, that's easy to relate to the Yozi because they're the geography there).<br /> <br /> I don't know what the authors are thinking to do, but it doesn't seem <i>contradictory </i>to conceptualize being the master of &quot;infernal related powers&quot; (including manifesting the will/power of the actual gods of hell), while not being extensions of two particular Yozi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T07:05:15-08:00","id":1555057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1555056#post1555056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I can see the issue that the OP sees, albeit I don't necessarily agree. I have a problem of extremes here:<br /> <br /> 2e Infernals were practically extensions of the Yozi that had to paint their individuality with the colours they were given (so to speak). That <i>does </i>give an &quot;infernal&quot; feel in that you're an extensions of the &quot;gods of hell&quot; (so to speak), but Infernals were supposed to have free will - you had the Akuma for being an extension of Yozi will. I can see how one would want Infernals to be &quot;impressive on their own right&quot;.<br /> <br /> But if the proposed solution it's doing a 180\u00b0, and trying to be as sepparate from the Yozi as possible, &quot;Yozi like but having <i>as little </i>to do with the actual Yozi as possible&quot;, then I would agree with the OP: That doesn't feel very &quot;infernal&quot; to me. I wouldn't like if Yozi get ignored, after all, they are the demon-gods. They're Hell itself. Every demon has something to do with them. They're important to the Lore in ways the average demon isn't (that they were the original creators of the world that want to come back it's <i>interesting</i>), being a disconnected &quot;Yozi-like creature&quot; is hardly going to fell as badass to me.<br /> <br /> That being said, I do think it's possible to get that &quot;prestigious infernal feel&quot; w/o needing to go back to 2ed where you were defined by your chosen Yozi patrons.<br /> <br /> Heck, the very OP proves it: Does summoning a manifestation of a Yozi suffices to make Siderals feel like &quot;good Infernalists&quot;? ... well, why shouldn't Infernals be able to do things like that? (<i>not the</i> <i>same thing</i>, mind you, but akin to it - ways to &quot;manifest/take power from Hell itself&quot;, that's easy to relate to the Yozi because they're the geography there).<br /> <br /> I don't know what the authors are thinking to do, but it doesn't seem <i>contradictory </i>to conceptualize being the master of &quot;infernal related powers&quot; (including manifesting the will/power of the actual gods of hell), while not being extensions of two particular Yozi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree there IS room for compromise, at least. I can absolutely see that there are ways to embody Yozi glory without compromising character agency when other nomic assumptions (like say, the Neverborn literally leashing the Abyssal Charmset) are being overhauled. I would have more confidence in whatever is supposed to replace that vision if how it has been primarily sold has been in that 180 degree, correction-for-correction's sake approach. I cannot stress enough how relieved I'd be to be proven wrong, that there is an intentionality present to portray how Infernals are not lesser than Solars for not having Yozi Charms, that the alien wonder of the Yozis will be well-demonstrated in Ability format, and that subsouls and (initially?) inner worlds will be something more than just a one-and-done curio with absolutely no further implications on the Infernal condition. That Infernals can, in fact, grow and develop in interesting ways as something other than the Solars but damned, even if they are no longer the Yozis' successors. I am in the market for good ideas.<br /> <br /> I just haven't seen any reason to believe in any. Rather, most of what I've seen regarding developer discourse about Infernals comes across as a reductive exercise, taking things away and de-emphasising the narrative conceits I was hoping for. I'd like to have hope, it's just hard to with what I do know. Unless I'm just supposed to ignore literally all of it, up to and including what's known about the castes and their natures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T07:09:48-08:00","id":1555058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1555027#post1555027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If your attachment to this thing is based on the perception of it having this kind of prestige, then it's not really great for emphasizing the Exalted characters.<br /> <br /> And just a general issue of serial escalation. Like, you're getting wildly out of proportion when it's reached the point of &quot;anything less than being actual God isn't worth it&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Infernal Exalted deserve to be impressive in their own right.<br /> <br /> As for the thread title question, no, a single example of Sidereal esoteric weirdness in the form of invoking Adorjan as a death effect does not make the Sidereal Exalted more evocative of this setting's Hell than the characters who are going to express demonic and Yozi qualities across the entire range of their powers. That would be like looking at the one Solar Charm to let them turn into a shadow and saying they're better at darkness than Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly disagree with both your statements. I felt 2e did a good job of emphasizing the Exalted through their removal to humanity rather than their embodiment of it-and like I said in the other post I AM open to new takes if they are compelling in their own right. And no, I am not asking for all Infernals to have omnipotent Charms baked in. In fact I feel you're mischaracterising my stance with hyperbole. <br /> <br /> Here is my rebuttal: I fail to see how the Infernal Exalted can be impressive in their own right, if (again, based on what has been said about them by the developers, and in published mateirals) as far as I can tell they will never allowed to escape the shadow of being broken Solars and nothing else. I see no Old Laws for them to master, no Metropoli-like advanced states (that are, again, not strictly speaking the Yozis per se in this thought exercise) to aspire towards, nothing as exciting as an SMA. Even the token premise of subsouls and inner worlds has more to prove in an edition where any sufficiently advanced sorcerer seems to have that well in their remit with sorcerous workings if, IF, there is nothing else to those concepts other than what is written.<br /> <br /> I will believe Infernals are better at expressing demonic and Yozi qualities when I actually see it, <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T12:10:22-08:00","id":1555064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1555056#post1555056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if the proposed solution it's doing a 180\u00b0, and trying to be as sepparate from the Yozi as possible, &quot;Yozi like but having <i>as little </i>to do with the actual Yozi as possible&quot;, then I would agree with the OP:</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe anybody has ever proposed that.<br /> <br /> Indeed, we have it from the writers that personality modification Charms will still be a thing, albeit without being the gateways for the larger Charm cascades. It's possible, likely even, that's the sort of thing I've argued against in the past, but honestly, good for everybody who liked that facet of the old design.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T12:20:14-08:00","id":1555065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Organ Boy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1555058#post1555058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is my rebuttal: I fail to see how the Infernal Exalted can be impressive in their own right, if (again, based on what has been said about them by the developers, and in published mateirals) as far as I can tell they will never allowed to escape the shadow of being broken Solars and nothing else. I see no Old Laws for them to master, no Metropoli-like advanced states (that are, again, not strictly speaking the Yozis per se in this thought exercise) to aspire towards, nothing as exciting as an SMA. Even the token premise of subsouls and inner worlds has more to prove in an edition where any sufficiently advanced sorcerer seems to have that well in their remit with sorcerous workings if, IF, there is nothing else to those concepts other than what is written.<br /> <br /> I will believe Infernals are better at expressing demonic and Yozi qualities when I actually see it,</div> </div> </div> </div>What... does &quot;mastering the Old Laws&quot; mean for high Essence Abyssals?<br /> <br /> And like, they have their devil-body transformations. That's pretty &quot;expressing demonic&quot; as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> Making the requirement of &quot;doesn't count if a sorcerer could theoretically do it&quot; is setting the goals pretty far afield, not least because there's a certain difference between a thing one could individually do at great effort and a thing that is an essential part of one's own nature. That and the fact that sorcery could probably do most of this stuff that you've otherwise regarded as proprietary.<br /> <br /> &quot;Broken Solar&quot; seems like a weird way to characterise it, as though to imply that they're lesser than the Solar Exalted. Like, they're still going to have freaky cool powers of their own. They'll probably be able to conjure up their Elfen Lied arms and such.<br /> <br /> Given the precedent of how Dragon-Blooded of all people have Charms with impressive environmental manifestations at high Essence, I think one can be fairly confident that the current developers will guide their writers towards similar things, scaled as appropriate to both being in the hands of peers of the Solar Exalted and the iconography of the Yozis.<br /> <br /> Bah, the Kickstarter is coming in a matter of weeks, I'm sure the matter will be resolved to mutual satisfaction then.<br /> <br /> (Alchemicals turning into cities is not an empowering experience for them, it's the ultimate expression of their theme of subordination to higher causes by having them fully subsume themselves as functions of their nation and God.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T11:26:45-08:00","id":1555131,"title":"","content":"As discussed on the same topic over on Sword of Creation, summoning a demon-prince to do a task isn't the same s embodying and using Yozi Charms. The Sidereal isn't using Yozi Charms anymore than an Infernal is. It's using a Charm to have a Yozi do a thing. The Charm isn't the Yozi, The Sidereal isn't becoming the Yozis. The Sidereal isn't becoming a mini-Yozi by using Yozi Charms like an Infernal was in 2e.<br /> <br /> The entire basis of this thread is built on the idea that one Sidereal power which has existed since before Infernals were even a thing somehow makes Sidereals better at channeling Hell's power. The entire premise stems from hyperbole on the idea that Infernals not being the literal embodiment of the Yozis and using the actual, literal same Charms as them, means they'll somehow not hae Hellish powers or things that draw on Exalted's unique Hell aesthetics. And that Sidereals getting one themed-around-the-rules-of-confinement power is somehow closer to the 2e Infernal Charm setup than what Infernals, who still by all accounts wield the power of Hell as inspired by the Yozis, are doing as their their main aesthetic framework.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T11:31:18-08:00","id":1555132,"title":"","content":"Note also that 3e has actually distanced the becoming cities element of Alchemicals. It is treated basically as character retirement if it were to happen, but is also so far past the actual gamed experience of most tables or the assumed game loop that it's htere more to give a weird way cities form than cosnidered this big transcendant element core to Alchemicals and some underlying transhuman themes of them. Again, it's a mountain out of a molehill. 2e Infernals treated the inhumantiy aspect of gaining alien power as some sort of big deal transhuman thing, while Alchemicals spends a lot of time trying to push that despite being magitech golems they are still very much human with human wants and needs, along with Clarity being actually presented as a thing they fight against on that. <br /> <br /> Saying Alchemicals get to be transhuman but Infernals don't is pretty superficial, dismissive of a lot of the themes of Alchemicals, and is not relaly clearw hat Infernals are doing that's transhuman besides &quot;Be less like an undderstnadable human through superpowers&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T11:41:03-08:00","id":1555133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1555027#post1555027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... And just a general issue of serial escalation. Like, you're getting wildly out of proportion when it's reached the point of &quot;anything less than being actual God isn't worth it&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Infernal Exalted deserve to be impressive in their own right.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>One more quote but this kind of summarizes how <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26460\" data-vbnamecard=\"26460\">Organ Boy</a> has characterized things so far in this. That Infernals needs to apparently basically be about not-Exalted (the Yozis) in order to be valid. That the Infernals thesmelves odn't matter unless they're just clones of the things that he seems to think actulaly matter (the Yozis). That hter'es no heat that one can build on the Infernal Exaltation, its own themes, and how Hell is filtered through that, rather than I guess the in effect micro-fiction psychology profiles of titans that 2e oftenw as.<br /> <br /> Like, this is again, a lot of hyperbole over one power Sidereals have, have always had, and never has been an issue in that context. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T17:33:55-08:00","id":1555143,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't want to get too into the weeds of what people mean about transhumanism for Internals or want out of it as a goal. To me, the main thing to dispute is to say that whether powers like Freedom Lets Go count as transhuman or not, their main function is the additional drama they lend to the ongoing journey of an Exalt rather than being a step in the end goal.<br /> <br /> And I think that end goal is going to be more concerned with accomplishing political and personal goals in Creation than some transformation into something beyond the setting not just because that really goes for most of the characters, but because it's a lot more rooted in the genre and style of Exalted. It draws inspiration from a style of fantasy concerned with being wilful and larger than life, and I think a focus on eventual transformation to something transcendent clashes severely with that. <br /> <br /> It frustrates me when people take it as a given that something focused on an objective of transcendence is superior as a matter of course to something focused on the objectives of grounded human beings. Like listening to a person assert that, logically, the (hypothetical) love of God must intrinsically be superior to all love between people, because it is elevated and eternal. As far as conventions of fiction go, it's just different rather than better. It doesn't do some things well, and there are some models of story it isn't suited to.<br /> <br /> That being said, I actually do think Infernals should have high Essence powers that come off as tools that could be applied towards a long term goal of transforming the metaphysical nature of the world. That's in terms of seeing Infernals as weird mystics rather than potential Yozis, but where the juxtaposition between their human scale and capacity to ultimately change the world emphasizes their uniqueness while giving nods to the origins of their power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T16:49:26-08:00","id":1555565,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, since we're less than 24 hours from the crowdfunding for the book going live here's a bunch of previewed Charm names.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Universal: Apocalypse King Apotheosis<br /> Awareness: Careless Cosmic Blink<br /> Brawl: Star-Swallowing Cosmos Collapse<br /> Bureaucracy: Mercurial Passion Mint<br /> Integrity: Adoring Atrocity Infatuation<br /> Linguistics: Hierarchic Logos Syntax<br /> Lore: Slumbering Prophet Revelation<br /> Medicine: I Alone Can Save You<br /> Occult: Universe-Forging Demiurge Omnipotence<br /> Sail: Raucous Scoundrel Revelry<br /> Socialize: Fiend to All Nations<br /> Survival: Behemoth Fetch Exercise<br /> Thrown: Cutting Down the Sky<br /> War: Splintered Gale Legion </div> </div> </div>How does that look for Charms that seem Infernalist or drawing on the nature of the creators of the world or whatever the complaint was?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T15:40:34-08:00","id":1555644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1555143#post1555143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't want to get too into the weeds of what people mean about transhumanism for Internals or want out of it as a goal. To me, the main thing to dispute is to say that whether powers like Freedom Lets Go count as transhuman or not, their main function is the additional drama they lend to the ongoing journey of an Exalt rather than being a step in the end goal.<br /> <br /> And I think that end goal is going to be more concerned with accomplishing political and personal goals in Creation than some transformation into something beyond the setting not just because that really goes for most of the characters, but because it's a lot more rooted in the genre and style of Exalted. It draws inspiration from a style of fantasy concerned with being wilful and larger than life, and I think a focus on eventual transformation to something transcendent clashes severely with that.<br /> <br /> It frustrates me when people take it as a given that something focused on an objective of transcendence is superior as a matter of course to something focused on the objectives of grounded human beings. Like listening to a person assert that, logically, the (hypothetical) love of God must intrinsically be superior to all love between people, because it is elevated and eternal. As far as conventions of fiction go, it's just different rather than better. It doesn't do some things well, and there are some models of story it isn't suited to.<br /> <br /> That being said, I actually do think Infernals should have high Essence powers that come off as tools that could be applied towards a long term goal of transforming the metaphysical nature of the world. That's in terms of seeing Infernals as weird mystics rather than potential Yozis, but where the juxtaposition between their human scale and capacity to ultimately change the world emphasizes their uniqueness while giving nods to the origins of their power.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1555143#post1555143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't want to get too into the weeds of what people mean about transhumanism for Internals or want out of it as a goal. To me, the main thing to dispute is to say that whether powers like Freedom Lets Go count as transhuman or not, their main function is the additional drama they lend to the ongoing journey of an Exalt rather than being a step in the end goal.<br /> <br /> And I think that end goal is going to be more concerned with accomplishing political and personal goals in Creation than some transformation into something beyond the setting not just because that really goes for most of the characters, but because it's a lot more rooted in the genre and style of Exalted. It draws inspiration from a style of fantasy concerned with being wilful and larger than life, and I think a focus on eventual transformation to something transcendent clashes severely with that.<br /> <br /> It frustrates me when people take it as a given that something focused on an objective of transcendence is superior as a matter of course to something focused on the objectives of grounded human beings. Like listening to a person assert that, logically, the (hypothetical) love of God must intrinsically be superior to all love between people, because it is elevated and eternal. As far as conventions of fiction go, it's just different rather than better. It doesn't do some things well, and there are some models of story it isn't suited to.<br /> <br /> That being said, I actually do think Infernals should have high Essence powers that come off as tools that could be applied towards a long term goal of transforming the metaphysical nature of the world. That's in terms of seeing Infernals as weird mystics rather than potential Yozis, but where the juxtaposition between their human scale and capacity to ultimately change the world emphasizes their uniqueness while giving nods to the origins of their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of your post comes across as completely incomprehensible and aggressively condescending to me, except insofar as it\u2019s describing a Heroic Mortals game. Yes, of course personal and political goals should be important in Exalted. But <i>so should the high concept stuff</i> otherwise you might as well argue SMAs, Solar Lore Charms and sorcery are all excessive and the game would be better off with them culled. I cannot reconcile the idea that the game somehow has greater artistic merit or something if it subtracts cool and interesting things from it, rather than attempt to strike a balance between the mythical and the mundane. Frankly, you come across like you\u2019re much more interested in what you think Exalted SHOULD be about than what it\u2019s sold as-and if we were talking about your campaign and only yours, that would be fair play. But we\u2019re not. I for one have never advocated for Exalted to be anything other than what the official published material presented it as. The only thing I really agree with you on is the last thing. <br /> <br /> Regardless, seeing as the backerkit\u2019s finally here I suppose this thread of mine is largely a moot point. As I said in the other thread, I\u2019m pleasantly surprised on a number of levels, and for reasons that have absolutely nothing to do with any of the points you argued.<br /> <br /> As for the Charms you listed, frankly I am reserving judgement until I actually see the rules for them. I\u2019ll never know if the current drafts were always the plan for Infernals or if a project stretching over literal years has changed it\u2019s overall design plan (although I would find it more odd if something this long in the pipeline DIDN\u2019T, at least a little), but frankly none of the information released beforehand prepared me for what\u2019s been presented so far. So I\u2019m simply choosing to keep an open mind and focus on what\u2019s set in stone-just, more optimistically than I was initially led to believe <i>by the developers themselves. </i>Unstoppable Magnus Approach, for example, might sound like an interesting Charm of epic scope\u2026and it\u2019s effect is giving you a single temporary Willpower at Lore 5 Essence 5.<br /> <br /> I still don\u2019t know what to expect anymore, but in a good way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T15:48:55-08:00","id":1555645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1555064#post1555064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't believe anybody has ever proposed that.<br /> <br /> Indeed, we have it from the writers that personality modification Charms will still be a thing, albeit without being the gateways for the larger Charm cascades. It's possible, likely even, that's the sort of thing I've argued against in the past, but honestly, good for everybody who liked that facet of the old design.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be blunt I have been under the impression you and Blaque are both taking this position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T18:07:20-08:00","id":1555651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1554906-3e-sidereals-better-infernalists-than-infernals?p=1555565#post1555565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, since we're less than 24 hours from the crowdfunding for the book going live here's a bunch of previewed Charm names.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How does that look for Charms that seem Infernalist or drawing on the nature of the creators of the world or whatever the complaint was?</div> </div> </div> </div>The initial complaint was that prior to the release of the draft, the impression I got from all published material and developer commentary is that Infernals would be Infernals in name only, and people like you were positing that as a good thing for some ineffable reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}